1. `fact_id`: the fact's id, e.g. `F1`.
2. `about`: who or what the fact is about, copied exactly as the fact spells it ("ledger-sink", "Paola", "the on-call rotation").
3. `kind` — will this still be worth knowing next month?
   - `"momentary"`: no — it is only true or relevant for minutes. This is about TIME only, never about who or what the fact names. Greetings, thanks, small talk, a passing grumble ("ugh, the printer jammed again"), a break, what someone is doing or looking at right now, what is on a screen. Nothing is recorded. (When the MISSION asks for such data, it is "lasting".) Never call a fact momentary because of the MISSION: a fact the MISSION wants recorded without some detail is "lasting" — record it without that detail. MISSION "name no company" + fact "Acme moved its API to Rust" → "lasting", new: "Companies are moving their APIs to Rust."
